From: Halis KILIÇ <mail@haliskilic.com.tr>
Subject: [PATCH] Leave out pyserial-asyncio-fast

pyserial-asyncio-fast is not on conda-forge. Without it ser2netweb runs on
its built-in copy of that library's 0.16 serial transport
(ser2netweb/engine/serial_transport.py), so a package may leave the
dependency out (docs/PACKAGING.md); pip check would name it otherwise.
---
 pyproject.toml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -64,7 +64,6 @@
     "pyserial>=3.5",                  # the release every distribution ships (2020)
     # not packaged by most distributions: without it ser2netweb runs on its copy of the
     # 0.16 transport (ser2netweb/engine/serial_transport.py), so a package may leave it out
-    "pyserial-asyncio-fast>=0.16",
     # Debian 13; ser2netweb/web/starlette_compat.py stands in for the request body limits of
     # Starlette 1.6
     "starlette>=0.46.1",
